{"authoritative_registration_status":"pending_coordinator_registration","candidate_id":"candidate.stacks.04458d2cb78e0e24ce3e67c8","decision":"source_equivalence_held","hold_classification":"raw_source_reference","hold_reason":"First clause retains raw Section \ref{section-representable} reference for the representable quasi-compact property instead of giving the scheme-base-change test. The generic editorial preface does not state the required exact quasi-compactness definition.","original_source_statement_tex":"\label{lemma-characterize-representable-quasi-compact}
Let $S$ be a scheme.
Let $f : X \to Y$ be a representable morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$.
The following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $f$ is quasi-compact
(in the sense of Section \ref{section-representable}), and
