The functor from left to right sends a presheaf $F$ to $\mathcal S_F$, whose objects are $(U,x)$ with $x\in F(U)$, and an arrow $(V,y)\to(U,x)$ over $f:V\to U$ exists exactly when $F(f)(x)=y$.
