source.original_statement_tex:
\label{lemma-stable-specialization}
Let $T \subset X$ be a subset of a topological space $X$.
The following are equivalent
\begin{enumerate}
\item $T$ is stable under specialization, and
\item $T$ is a (directed) union of closed subsets of $X$.
\end{enumerate}

\label{lemma-Jacobson-universally-Jacobson}
Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a Jacobson algebraic space over $S$.
Any algebraic space locally of finite type over $X$ is Jacobson.

