{"approved_content_sha256":"31136a2ae28e2d062cd3bcc3d80296606fb937eea2f1d8f94d4fb754d146d0fd","batch_id":"p2f-w2-b012","candidate_id":"candidate.stacks.7942678b61d42281197e6dea","decision":"source_equivalence_approved","final_content":{"conclusions":["Canonical module support is maximal-dimensional components and satisfies S2."],"equivalence_sides":null,"hypotheses":["Normalized Noetherian local A, d=dim A, ω_A=H^{-d} dualizing."],"logical_form":"multiple_canonical_module_conclusions","statement":"Let $(A,\mathfrak m,\kappa)$ be a Noetherian local ring, with a *normalized* dualizing complex $\omega_A^\bullet$: this is a dualizing complex satisfying $R\operatorname{Hom}_A(\kappa,\omega_A^\bullet)\simeq\kappa[0]$. For an $A$-module $M$ put $\operatorname{Ext}_A^i(M,\omega_A^\bullet)=H^i(R\operatorname{Hom}_A(M,\omega_A^\bullet))$. Let $d=\dim A$ and define the *dualizing module* (canonical module of $A$) by $\omega_A=H^{-d}(\omega_A^\bullet)$, a finite $A$-module. Then (1) $\operatorname{Supp}_A(\omega_A)$ is exactly the union of irreducible components $V(\mathfrak p)$ with $\mathfrak p$ minimal and $\dim(A/\mathfrak p)=d$; and (2) $\omega_A$ satisfies Serre condition $(S_2)$ as a module: for every $\mathfrak p$, $\operatorname{depth}_{A_{\mathfrak p}}(\omega_A)_{\mathfrak p}\ge\min\{2,\dim\operatorname{Supp}_{A_{\mathfrak p}}(\omega_A)_{\mathfrak p}\}$. This is a module statement even if $A$ is not Cohen–Macaulay.","structured_cases":null},"original_source_statement_tex":"\label{lemma-depth-dualizing-module}
Let $(A, \mathfrak m, \kappa)$ be a Noetherian local ring with
normalized dualizing complex $\omega_A^\bullet$. Let $d = \dim(A)$
and $\omega_A = H^{-d}(\omega_A^\bullet)$. Then
\begin{enumerate}
\item the support of $\omega_A$ is the union of the irreducible components
of $\Spec(A)$ of dimension $d$,
