{"authoritative_registration_status":"pending_coordinator_registration","candidate_id":"candidate.stacks.ad98274708835212ffb11598","decision":"source_equivalence_held","hold_classification":"ambiguous_itemwise_logical_form","hold_reason":"For a cofiltered spectral diagram there are two conditional consequences: nonempty compatible constructible-closed Z_i have nonempty limit; nonempty X_i have nonempty full limit. Stage B 'itemwise_claims_or_equivalence' permits an incorrect equivalence interpretation.","original_source_statement_tex":"\label{lemma-inverse-limit-spectral-spaces-nonempty}
Let $\mathcal{I}$ be a cofiltered category. Let $i \mapsto X_i$ be a diagram
of spectral spaces such that for $a : j \to i$ in $\mathcal{I}$
the corresponding map $f_a : X_j \to X_i$ is spectral.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Given nonempty subsets $Z_i \subset X_i$ closed in the constructible
topology with $f_a(Z_j) \subset Z_i$ for all $a : j \to i$ in $\mathcal{I}$,
